      "structure_description": "One of seven isomorphous, discrete tetrameric polyoxoanions. Two symmetric organotin–Ce2–Te2–W18 units, each incorporating two tetravacant B-α-TeW8O31 subunits and an isonicotinate-decorated W2O4 segment, are joined by two acetate connectors.",
      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "ph": "4.5, adjusted with 6 mol L−1 HCl",
        "procedure": "Dissolve sodium tungstate dihydrate, potassium tellurite, isonicotinic acid, dimethylamine hydrochloride, and glacial acetic acid in distilled water with stirring. After 10 min, add Ce(NO3)3·6H2O and dimethyltin dichloride consecutively. Adjust the final pH to 4.5, stir for another 10 min, heat at 90 °C for 2 h, cool, and filter.",
        "reagents": [
          {
            "amount": "2.003 g, 6.060 mmol",
            "formula": "Na2WO4·2H2O",
            "name": "sodium tungstate dihydrate",
            "role": "tungstate source"
          },
          {
